### Feature Users — GET ALL / GET ONE (modalidad JWT + RBAC)
### JWT + RBAC: `authenticate` (401 si no hay identidad válida) +
### `authorize` (403 si la matriz no concede el par method+path).
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/session/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "admin",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.access_token}}
@id = 1

### getAll — recurso `GET /api/users` (solo ADMIN). Nunca devuelve `password`.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### getOne — recurso `GET /api/users/:id`
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Permisos efectivos de un usuario — recurso `GET /api/users/:id/permissions`
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{id}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 400 — id no es entero positivo (validado en BaseController.paramId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 401 — sin token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users

### 403 — el rol MEDICO no tiene concedido `GET /api/users`
# @name loginMedico
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/session/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "medico",
  "password": "Medico123!"
}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMedico.response.body.$.access_token}}
